<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:32:default:windows">
<!--
    kuna issue testcase: a `rep movsd` that copies a by-value struct into the
    outgoing argument area with a known count is expanded before the stack is
    heritaged (`p3_dataflow/kuna_repframecopy.rs`, always on; `indexaliasguard
    off` turns it off with the other stack guards).

    Issue:      kuna GH-1562 - x86-32 MSVC: a by-value struct argument copied
                with `rep movsd` makes the call that takes it print with no
                arguments, and a pushed return address prints as a value.
    Stage:      P3 dataflow - right after the first heritage pass, before the
                stack's first heritage (`ActionHeritage`).
    P0 assert:  none (a strict fix); one pass.

    byval_pe_i386.exe (VC8 /O2, notes in byval_pe_i386.txt), draw (0x401000):
    paint(a, b, 3), then `Rect r = *src` (rep movsd into a local) and
    `fill(r, b)` (`sub esp,0x20; mov edi,esp; rep movsd` into the outgoing
    area). Before: `v9 = 0x401018;` (paint's pushed return address), two
    `while` copy loops and `sub_401070()`. Now fill takes r's eight dwords and
    b, paint keeps its three arguments, and neither the loops nor the return
    address are left.
    repframecopy_pe_i386.exe (clean-room asm, notes in repframecopy_pe_i386.asm):
    ebp_draw (0x401070, frame pointer, a branch before the copies) passes src's
    eight dwords and b to fill8; forward (0x401130) passes its own by-value
    parameter on; the entry (0x401180) passes a global table by value, and its
    other calls keep their pushed arguments. Left as loops: big_pass (0x4010b0,
    32 dwords, too large), copy_global (0x4010d0, no frame slot), zero_pass
    (0x4010f0, the copy reads a local a `rep stosd` walks) and loop_fill
    (0x401150, the copy reads a local an indexed loop writes).
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
